+# Hegel property-based testing report: hcl-rs (fable)
+
+Target: `crates/hcl-rs` (lib name `hcl`, v0.19.7) in the martinohmann/hcl-rs
+workspace, plus its `hcl-primitives` dependency (where several root causes
+live). hegeltest 0.28.2 added as a dev-dependency of `hcl-rs`; `serde_json`
+dev-dependency gained the `float_roundtrip` feature so it is an exact float
+oracle. Consent check: no AI-contribution gate found (CONTRIBUTING.md is
+standard; no HUMAN_VS_MACHINE.md / .ai-ack / anti-AI license clause).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+Tests live in the existing integration-test files; shared generators in
+`tests/common/mod.rs` (`gen` module: `tricky_strings` at the escape boundary,
+`escape_safe_strings`, `idents` incl. keywords/dashes/unicode, `safe_numbers`,
+recursive `exprs`/`bodies`/`values`, `top_level_values`).
+
+`tests/ser.rs`:
+1. **Body serialize→parse fixpoint** (`prop_body_serialize_parse_fixpoint`) —
+   arbitrary `Body` (attributes with unique keys, nested blocks with
+   ident/string labels, expressions over null/bool/number/string/array/object)
+   → `hcl::to_string` → `hcl::parse` → equality AND re-serialized text
+   fixpoint.
+2. **Value serialize→parse fixpoint** (`prop_value_serialize_parse_fixpoint`) —
+   same for `hcl::Value` trees via `hcl::from_str::<Value>`.
+3. **String escaping roundtrip** (`prop_string_escape_roundtrip`) — strings
+   built from escape-boundary tokens (`${`, `%{`, `$${`, quotes, backslashes,
+   control chars, NEL/LS/PS, unicode) as attribute values. **KNOWN FAILURE**
+   (bug 3 below).
+4. **Keyword object keys roundtrip** (`prop_keyword_object_keys_roundtrip`) —
+   object keys `true`/`false`/`null`/`for`. **KNOWN FAILURE** (bug 4).
+5. **Number serialize→parse roundtrip** (`prop_number_serialize_parse_roundtrip`)
+   — i64/u64/f64 numbers keep value and int-vs-float type through text.
+6. **`Number::from_f64` value preservation** (`prop_number_from_f64_roundtrips_value`)
+   — `from_f64(f).as_f64() == Some(f)` for finite f. **KNOWN FAILURE** (bug 2).
+7. **JSON interop** (`prop_value_json_roundtrip`) — `Value` →
+   `serde_json::to_string` → `Value` is identity (serde_json with
+   `float_roundtrip` as exact oracle).
+
+`tests/de.rs`:
+8. **Parse robustness** (`prop_parse_never_panics_on_arbitrary_text`,
+   `prop_parse_never_panics_on_hcl_shaped_text`) — `hcl::parse` /
+   `hcl::from_str::<Value>` never panic on arbitrary unicode text or on
+   HCL-fragment soup (unclosed heredocs, dangling markers, operators).
+9. **Deep-nesting robustness** (`prop_parse_never_panics_on_nested_input`) —
+   sweeps depth 0..=40 across 6 nesting shapes (the sweep space is small
+   enough that hegel exhausted all 246 combinations at high case count);
+   capped at 40 because of bug 1, which is pinned by the `#[ignore]`d
+   reproducer `deeply_nested_input_overflows_stack`.
+10. **Negated integer literals are non-positive**
+    (`prop_parse_negated_integer_literal_is_nonpositive`) — `a = -N` for u64
+    N must not parse to a positive number. **KNOWN FAILURE** (bug 5; also the
+    debug-build panic for N = 2^63).
+11. **`from_body` / text-route agreement**
+    (`prop_from_body_agrees_with_parsing_serialized_body`) —
+    `hcl::from_body::<Value>(body)` equals
+    `hcl::from_str::<Value>(&hcl::to_string(&body))` (exercises the HCL JSON
+    spec block-merging on both routes).
+12. **Attribute vs block disambiguation**
+    (`prop_attribute_vs_block_disambiguation`) — for any identifier k
+    (keywords, dashes, unicode): `k = {}` is an attribute, `k {}` / `k lbl {}`
+    are blocks with the right identifier/labels.
+
+`tests/format.rs`:
+13. **Format-trait Value roundtrip** (`prop_format_value_roundtrip`) —
+    `hcl::format::to_string(&value)` embedded as an attribute expression
+    re-parses to an equal `Value`. **KNOWN FAILURE** (bug 6).
+
+`tests/template.rs`:
+14. **Template parse robustness** (`prop_template_parse_never_panics`) —
+    `Template::from_str` on arbitrary/template-shaped text, and the same text
+    embedded as a quoted attribute value, never panic.
+
+## Test results
+
+`cargo test -p hcl-rs --no-fail-fast`: everything passes **except** the five
+deliberately failing KNOWN-FAILURE pins (properties 3, 4, 6, 10, 13) and one
+`#[ignore]`d process-aborting reproducer. All pins fail deterministically
+(boosted generators / sampled counterexamples). Liveness was verified by
+inverting the body-fixpoint assertion (hegel shrank to `Body([])`) and
+reverting; a 10x exploratory run (test_cases = 1000, verified with case
+counters: 1104 body-fixpoint cases) surfaced no additional failures beyond
+those below.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+All are oracle-independent (panic, abort, or roundtrip corruption of an input
+we still hold). Not yet deduped against the upstream issue tracker.
+
+1. **Stack overflow / process abort on deeply nested input** (`hcl-edit`
+   parser, reached via `hcl::parse`). On a 2 MiB test thread the process
+   aborts at depth ~100 for nested objects (`{b={b=...}}`) and blocks, ~150
+   for arrays, ~200 for parens and unary minus chains (debug build). A DoS
+   vector for the documented untrusted-input entry point. Pinned by
+   `deeply_nested_input_overflows_stack` (`#[ignore]`d — cannot be caught).
+   (An old pest-era performance issue may be related; the current
+   winnow-based parser still recurses unboundedly.)
+2. **`Number::from_f64` silently corrupts whole-valued floats ≥ 2^63**
+   (`hcl-primitives/src/number.rs`, `N::from_finite_f64`): `value.fract()==0`
+   routes through a *saturating* `value as i64` cast, so
+   `from_f64(1e300)` → `9223372036854775807` and `from_f64(-1e300)` →
+   `-9223372036854775808`. Corrupts `Value::from(f64)`, serde serialization
+   of large float fields, and parsing of literals like `1e300`. Shrunk
+   counterexample: `9.223372036854778e18`.
+3. **`escape_markers` mis-escapes `$`/`%` runs before `{`**
+   (`hcl-primitives/src/template.rs`, `escape_markers_owned`): the scanner
+   consumes `$`/`%` pairs blindly, so in `"${$${"` the second marker is left
+   unescaped: it serializes to `"$${$${"`, which parses back as `"${${"` —
+   silent string-value corruption on a plain serialize→parse roundtrip.
+   Mixed runs (`"${$%{"`) even produce *unparseable* output. Correct output
+   would be `"$${$$${"`.
+4. **Keyword object keys serialize to text that changes meaning**:
+   `ObjectKey::Identifier("true")` serializes bare as `{ true = ... }` and
+   re-parses as `ObjectKey::Expression(Bool(true))`; `hcl::from_str::<Value>`
+   then *errors* ("invalid type: boolean `true`, expected a string") while
+   `hcl::from_body` on the original body succeeds. An object key `for`
+   serializes to `{ for = ... }`, which does not parse at all (for-expression
+   ambiguity). The serializer should quote these keys.
+5. **Unary minus on large integer literals wraps/saturates**
+   (`hcl-primitives` `N::neg` + parse-time folding):
+   `a = -9223372036854775808` (i64::MIN!) **panics** with "attempt to negate
+   with overflow" in debug builds — i.e. `parse(to_string(body))` panics for
+   a body holding `i64::MIN`; `a = -9223372036854775809` parses as
+   **+9223372036854775807**; `a = -18446744073709551615` parses as **+1**.
+   The silent sign-flips reproduce in release builds too.
+6. **`Format`-path `Value` serialization emits invalid HCL for
+   template-looking strings**: `Format for Value` writes strings for which
+   `is_templated` is true verbatim (`src/format/impls.rs`), but
+   `is_templated` does not validate the template, so
+   `hcl::format::to_string(&Value::String("${x".into()))` produces `"${x"`,
+   which fails to re-parse. (The serde path `hcl::to_string` escapes instead
+   — the two serializers disagree about template preservation.)
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **serde_json as float oracle without `float_roundtrip`**: the JSON interop
+  property initially "failed" on `0.9500391205085137` → `...136`. That is
+  serde_json's documented default fast-path float parsing, not an hcl bug;
+  fixed by enabling the `float_roundtrip` feature on the dev-dependency
+  rather than weakening the property.
+- No property was weakened beyond the documented exclusions: sibling
+  generators exclude i64::MIN, whole floats ≥ 2^63, `$`/`%`-run escape
+  sequences, and keyword object keys — each exclusion carries a comment
+  naming the canonical pinned test for the bug it avoids.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The escape-boundary guidance ("generate at the encode-set boundary") was
+  directly decisive: bug 3 was found immediately by concatenating boundary
+  tokens; uniform text had not hit it.
+- The "probe recursion depth directly" and "sweep depth" advice found the
+  stack overflow in the first probe run; the observed threshold (~100 on a
+  2 MiB thread) confirms the skill's warning that test threads overflow far
+  earlier than main threads.
+- The serde_json float-oracle trap happened exactly as the skill's "audit a
+  floating-point oracle" note predicts (1-ULP disagreement, opt-in
+  round-trip mode); the note made triage instant.
+- The depth×shape sweep space (41×6) was exhausted by hegel at high case
+  count — a nice confirmation the engine enumerates small discrete spaces,
+  worth mentioning in the reference as a way to get exhaustive coverage of
+  small sweeps for free.
+- Friction: `one_of!` branches mixing a `#[hegel::composite]` generator with
+  `.boxed()` generators unified without explicit boxing of the composite —
+  the reference's "box only if the compiler demands" wording was accurate.
